---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---
<Docs title="Deployment — otlp-c docs">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-50">Deployment</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-slate-400">
    otlp-c speaks plain HTTP to a local collector. TLS, queueing, and
    fan-out belong to that collector — the
    <a href="/use-cases/" class="text-teal-300 underline decoration-ink-700">sidecar topology</a>
    is the production shape.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100">The topology</h2>
  <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/60 p-8">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 760 240" class="mx-auto min-w-[680px]" role="img" aria-label="Sidecar topology">
      <defs>
        <marker id="arr" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto">
          <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" fill="#5eead4" />
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <!-- app -->
      <rect x="20" y="60" width="200" height="120" rx="12" fill="#1a2138" stroke="#26304d" />
      <text x="120" y="105" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e2e8f0" font-family="monospace" font-size="14">your application</text>
      <rect x="45" y="120" width="150" height="34" rx="8" fill="#14b8a6" fill-opacity="0.15" stroke="#14b8a6" stroke-opacity="0.5"/>
      <text x="120" y="142" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5eead4" font-family="monospace" font-size="12">otlp-c (in-proc)</text>
      <!-- sidecar -->
      <rect x="280" y="60" width="200" height="120" rx="12" fill="#1a2138" stroke="#26304d" />
      <text x="380" y="105" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e2e8f0" font-family="monospace" font-size="14">otelcol sidecar</text>
      <text x="380" y="132" text-anchor="middle" fill="#94a3b8" font-family="monospace" font-size="11">TLS · retry · fan-out</text>
      <!-- backends -->
      <rect x="540" y="20" width="200" height="44" rx="8" fill="#0f1526" stroke="#26304d" />
      <text x="640" y="47" text-anchor="middle" fill="#94a3b8" font-family="monospace" font-size="12">Tempo / Jaeger</text>
      <rect x="540" y="98" width="200" height="44" rx="8" fill="#0f1526" stroke="#26304d" />
      <text x="640" y="125" text-anchor="middle" fill="#94a3b8" font-family="monospace" font-size="12">Honeycomb / Datadog</text>
      <rect x="540" y="176" width="200" height="44" rx="8" fill="#0f1526" stroke="#26304d" />
      <text x="640" y="203" text-anchor="middle" fill="#94a3b8" font-family="monospace" font-size="12">S3 / anything OTLP</text>
      <!-- wires -->
      <line x1="220" y1="120" x2="280" y2="120" stroke="#5eead4" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
      <text x="250" y="110" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5eead4" font-family="monospace" font-size="10">:4318</text>
      <line x1="480" y1="90" x2="540" y2="48" stroke="#5eead4" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
      <line x1="480" y1="120" x2="540" y2="120" stroke="#5eead4" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
      <line x1="480" y1="150" x2="540" y2="192" stroke="#5eead4" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
      <text x="510" y="176" text-anchor="middle" fill="#94a3b8" font-family="monospace" font-size="10">TLS</text>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100">Kubernetes patterns</h2>
  <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/60 p-5">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-100">DaemonSet node agent</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
        One otelcol per node; every pod points at the node IP. Configure
        with one env var — the base endpoint:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-ink-700 bg-ink-950 p-3 font-mono text-[11.5px] text-slate-300"><code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://$NODE_IP:4318</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/60 p-5">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-100">Pod sidecar</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
        An otelcol container beside the app — same pod network:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-ink-700 bg-ink-950 p-3 font-mono text-[11.5px] text-slate-300"><code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4318</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100">Local development</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
    The repo ships the exact topology the CI integration runs:
  </p>
  <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-ink-700 bg-ink-950 p-5 font-mono text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-slate-300"><code>cd tests/integration
docker compose up -d      # otelcol :4318 + Jaeger :16686
# run any example, then:
open http://localhost:16686/search?service=demo</code></pre>

  <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100">Why no TLS in-library</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
    A TLS dependency would violate the zero-non-libc constraint that
    makes the library embeddable in kernels and firmware, and every
    supported platform's native TLS stack is platform-specific anyway.
    The collector sidecar terminates TLS to real backends — one
    auditable place for certificates, mTLS, and retries. This is a
    recorded design decision (ADR-0004).
  </p>
</Docs>
